<title>RUSSIA: Russia 704-day OFZ bond tranche priced 102.06 pct. [CORRECTED 16:00 GMT]</title>
<headline>Russia 704-day OFZ bond tranche priced 102.06 pct. [CORRECTED 16:00 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Corrects headline and the text to show the tenor of the bond as 704-day instead of 702-day.)</p>
<p>The average price on a 704-day additional tranche of OFZ interest-bearing bonds with a fixed 20 percent coupon was 102.06 percent at auction on Wednesday, the central bank said.</p>
<p>Dealers had forecast the average price to be in the 102.15-102.35 percent range.</p>
<p>The original issue on Tuesday closed at 102.21 percent to yield 18.47 percent.</p>
<p>Full details of the auction follow:  </p>
<p>Series number (additional tranche)  25001</p>
<p>    Issue volume				2.50 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations			     1.00 million</p>
<p>    Bids (nominal)			    2.28 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Bids (sold)				 2.33 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Sold					  875.71 bln rbls</p>
<p>    Proceeds				    906.22 bln rbls</p>
<p>    Average price			     102.06 pct</p>
<p>    Lowest accepted price		   102.00 pct</p>
<p>    Average yield				18.56 pct</p>
<p>    Highest accepted yield		   18.60 pct</p>
<p>    Tenor (remaining)			  704 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date				June 6, 1999</p>
<p>    First coupon date			  June 6, 1998</p>
<p>The Finance Ministry will offer on Wednesday nine trillion roubles of 364-day GKO discount Treasury bills (series 21078).</p>
<p>It will also repay about 8.29 trillion roubles in maturing 203-day T-bill issue (series 22062).</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
